[[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Release by proper tool rear stop pins of boot covering.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Scraper blade</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.823.015.000</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Lower higher covering (2a) and disconnect electric connection\n(2b) of boot wiring.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>2b</p></td><td><p>Boot / rear coupling</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3235796\">D40</a></p></td></tr></table></div><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018621.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,0,"<p>1. DIsconnect electric connections (1a,1b,1c).</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1a</p></td><td><p>Left rear. light cluster on (moving section\nof boot)</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236018\">F35</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Rear lights cluster right (moving part on boot\nlid)</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236021\">F36</a></p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1c</p></td><td><p>Boot opening switch</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/3236227\">I11</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Extract wiring stop springs.</p><p>3. Extract fairlead sleeve by both sides.</p><p>4. Extract wiring from boot cap.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2018622.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2047,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check wiring is not damaged\nand each single conductor is properly anchored to connections.</p><p>Insert wiring in boot cap.</p><p>Put wiring stop springs on.</p><p>Connect electric connections.</p><p>Test functionality of connected electric\ncomponents.</p><p>Bind higher covering rear stop pins.</p>"]]